{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>He is holy to HaShem.</b> He merits to shine in the light of life and to be prepared to understand and instruct fittingly regarding the holy matters of the generation. It appears that Elkanah intended this when he said: אַךְ יָקֵם ה׳ אֶת דְּבָרוֹ (1 Samuel 1:23) — meaning: I consent to impose naziriteship upon him, and I ask nothing else from the blessed El on the child's behalf except that He establish His word, that he be holy to HaShem."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:49.082849251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}